UID:10000886-1796983200-1796986800@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Nature Tales Story Time
DESCRIPTION:Bring your little one for a morning or afternoon of stories\, songs\, and outdoor discovery! Nature Tales is a monthly family program for children ages 3-7 and a grown-up\, where a nature-themed story comes to life through hands-on exploration in the garden.\n Who? Children ages 3-7\, with an adult When? 10 a.m. to 11 a.m. or 3:30 p.m. to 4:30 p.m. Where? North Carolina Botanical Garden Cost? $5 per child (free for members and families receiving SNAP benefits) \nKnow a family who’d love this? Share the event!  \nUpcoming Dates: \nFriday\, December 11th – Where Did Everyone Go? \nWhere do animals go when winter arrives? Some migrate\, some hibernate\, some stay busy all winter\, and some find cozy places to hide. After the story\, head outside to look for clues that animals are still around\, even when we don’t see them! The program will happen rain or shine\, with indoor activities if the weather is unfavorable. Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nMore dates to come! Check back soon.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-story-time/2026-12-11/1/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/11/IMG_5861-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
