UID:10000885-1797674400-1797681600@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Tour of Coker Aboretum
DESCRIPTION:with Geoffrey Neal\, Curator\, Coker Arboretum \n  \nDiscover this five-acre gem in the heart of the UNC campus! Established in 1903\, Coker Arboretum is part of the North Carolina Botanical Garden and features a diverse collection of plants\, including flowering trees and shrubs\, bulbs\, and perennials. Join a Coker Arboretum curator for a winter walking tour and explore the history and beauty of this beloved garden. \nOffered each season\, every tour reveals something new as the Coker Arboretum changes throughout the year. \n  \nRegister here!\n  \nAccessibility:  \nThis is an outdoor tour that follows mostly flat pathways\, including brick and smooth or compacted grit surfaces.  After rains\, grit paths may become uneven\, eroded\, or soggy\, which may affect ease of travel. Participants are welcome to move at their own pace and take breaks as needed. We’ll be happy to discuss your needs and determine how we can best support your participation.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/coker-arboretum-tour/
LOCATION:Coker Arboretum\, 399 E. Cameron Avenue\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hikes and Tours
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/11/112922_0305-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.9131808;-79.0483369
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Coker Arboretum 399 E. Cameron Avenue Chapel Hill NC 27514 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=399 E. Cameron Avenue:geo:-79.0483369,35.9131808
END:VEVENT
